## AMEND-016 (2026-09-16, executor, PE_935_NIF_10_1_WORKAUDIT_CORRECTION_R1 — external WORK-AUDIT counterexample REPRODUCED; BABYLENGUIN XPU witness RETRACTED; field-identity tooling defect CONFIRMED and fixed by successor tooling)
- AUTHORITY: human-delivered correction contract (verbatim above); PE-MASTER dispatch with governance addenda. BASE verified: HEAD==origin==ls-remote==91e2af0249f4242cf41eb1f96bc8a1a7f3e63839; 2 pre-existing untracked roots untouched; ZERO git operations by executor.
- WHAT (science): the external WORK-AUDIT counterexample against F-17's READING ("BABYLENGUIN.NIF fails at block 7 GroupID=479309 — a NONZERO engine GroupID, POSITIVE realism evidence") is REPRODUCED INDEPENDENTLY from physical bytes. Fresh engine-transcribed byte walker (NEW SCRIPT s15_babylenguin_boundary_walker.py, SHA 19C168C6F089193825B08D90804672FB2F091C6480CF31E8AE9AD3E497FC2CA2, 21,232B; field sequences hand-transcribed from SRC-06 Gamebryo 1.2 engine source; NO s04/s06 schema machinery, NO external offsets; 3 executed negative controls: truncated input / corrupted string length / wrong version all fail as designed): BABYLENGUIN.NIF (1,737,966B, SHA256 A86C49384E62DF41339101B62E48BE6DCAE10E06B5F7CAC39DC627CF89635EA9) block 5 NiTexturingProperty 1408-1464 (TextureCount=7; slot[5]=BUMP HasMap=0 -> BumpMap extras NOT read — C1A VALUE-condition honored, VERSION != VALUE); block 6 NiSourceTexture 1464-1517: UseExternal=0 (INTERNAL), File Name 'LEN-SKIN_02.BMP' (15B @1485), PixelData link=7 -> block 7 NiPixelData, PixelLayout=6, UseMipmaps=1, AlphaFormat=3, IsStatic=1; REAL block 7 (NiPixelData) GroupID = 0 @1517. The 479309 value (0x0007504D; single occurrence in the file) = bytes @1498-1501 = filename tail 'M','P' + low 2 bytes of the pixel-data link (07 00) — NOT a GroupID. F-17's READING is RETRACTED (F-18 appended; F-17 original text byte-unchanged with a supersession pointer). The GroupID FRAMING verdicts (F-02/F-03/C-01 core: engine range 5.0.0.6<=v<10.1.0.114; physical presence; modern mis-version; historical omission) are UNAFFECTED — existence rests on engine source + physical slot reads, not on the retracted nonzero sample.
- WHAT (tooling root cause, CONFIRMED): frozen s06 SchemaDecoder._fields_for (L106-115) deduplicates effective schema fields by BARE FIELD NAME (first occurrence wins unless strictly higher version-preference) — FIELD_NAME was treated as FIELD_IDENTITY. NiSourceTexture's two conditional alternatives ('File Name'[cond Use External == 1] and 'File Name'[cond Use External == 0, ver1=10.1.0.0]) are both version-applicable at 10.1.0.0; the dedup keeps the first and LOSES the second, so for Use External == 0 blocks the filename bytes are never consumed -> boundary shift -> interior bytes misread as the next GroupID. Executed negative control (NEW SCRIPT s16_field_identity_mechanism_repro.py, SHA DD2667D14573FEDAC4C34522AD733F5E8267F43713CB22A0F220BFCFBB9C07AD, 7,492B): OLD model -> block 6 end=1498, "block 7 GroupID"=479309@1498 [REPRODUCED exactly]; V2 model -> block 6 end=1517, block 7 GroupID=0@1517 [PASS]; V2 effective list retains BOTH File Name occurrences.
- WHAT (fix): NEW SCRIPT s13_schema_field_identity_v2.py (SHA E3368507FCA5E9FDAE2AEADC1F9A55137DAEE242FBBDB5F410027C64455B4893, 12,487B) — FIELD_IDENTITY_V2 schema model + duplicate-name census; NEW SCRIPT s14_world_slice_validator_fieldidentity_v2.py (SHA 464D07E5203A8BA1D95ED1B3A5B94C6A932A8AABF979903490C893DD94293C04, 3,458B) — successor decoder subclassing the frozen s06 with ONLY _fields_for replaced (occurrence-preserving; identity = owner_type + field_name + occurrence_index + field_type + ver1 + ver2 + vercond + cond + template + schema_order; conditional alternatives remain distinct until value-condition evaluation). Historical scripts s01-s12 byte-unchanged; frozen holdout/hypothesis sha 6DB2F1E37E900A2573FEE07B5945B5E25B438066EA0A26AF0841540C96693752 NOT rewritten — s13/s14 SUPERSEDE TOOLING BEHAVIOR, DO NOT REWRITE HISTORICAL HOLDOUT.
- WHAT (measured blast radius):
  (a) C2 census (s13; 01_RAW/DUPLICATE_FIELD_IDENTITY_CENSUS.csv, 302 rows): 148 duplicate-name groups / 302 occurrences / 58 effective types in HIST 0.7.1.1; 21 groups LOAD-BEARING at 10.1.0.0; load-bearing types PHYSICALLY OBSERVED in PCG: NiSourceTexture (File Name x2), NiPSysData/NiMeshPSysData/NiTriShapeData (Num Vertices x2, type-name conds — in-slice byte-neutral for concrete NiTriShapeData; PSys family latent, non-slice); TexSource compound File Name x2 is an ORPHAN (no niobject references it).
  (b) C5 NiSourceTexture regression (NEW SCRIPT s17_nisourcetexture_fieldidentity_regression.py, SHA 3B93C8987B7072D0E6A232FB643D46B9A7F6C0EAFEB676B1014311A4DD998FEF, 17,818B; independent BNT2 walk + header scan of all 4,838 v10.1 payloads; bounded engine-transcribed readers for the controller/keyframe prefix types): denominator recomputed = 45 blocks / 5 files (matches prior expectation); 45/45 PASS under V2 — R1 external branch 44 blocks (File Name[UE==1] consumed; link=-1); R2 internal branch 1 block (204828.nif blk159: UE=0, FN='NPC_Animals_scaboreas_01_01.tga', link=160 -> NiPixelData, next gid=0) — the single block the OLD model would have mis-consumed; R3 denominator 45/0/0 PASS/FAIL/AMBIGUOUS. Full-file closure of 3/5 files still FAILS for reasons OUTSIDE NiSourceTexture (unsupported controller/PSys types — the frozen decoder family's known non-slice limitation; recorded per row, no hidden failures). Evidence: 01_RAW/NISOURCETEXTURE_FIELDIDENTITY_REGRESSION.csv.
  (c) C6 world-slice regression (NEW SCRIPT s18_world_slice_fieldidentity_regression.py, SHA 50BFA724B741075C0DAF5C56471498DC72DC15D93FD2CFBA22FE808481620FD9, 8,243B; frozen s06 re-executed read-only vs s14 V2 over all 2,363 slice files, single deterministic pass): PASS 2,343 + FAIL 20 + AMBIGUOUS 0 + INFRA_UNRESOLVED 0 = 2,363 (algebra closes; 0 infra stops — an infrastructure timeout is NOT a scientific failure; none occurred). OLD re-run reproduces the frozen run bit-exactly (2,343 closures; the SAME 20 blocked files: 12 ArkBlockError search-exhausted + 8 struct.error EOF). V2 = IDENTICAL on all 2,363: files_same_closure 2,363; files_newly_closing 0; files_newly_failing 0; files_ambiguous 0; changed_boundaries 0; changed_field_interpretations 0 (per-block [start,end] arrays + canonical value fingerprints compared). In-slice frozen measurements remain VALID under the corrected instrument. Evidence: 01_RAW/WORLD_SLICE_FIELDIDENTITY_REGRESSION.csv (2,363 rows); 02_ANALYSIS/FIELD_IDENTITY_V2_BLAST_RADIUS.md.
